type: software
title: "Reconstructing built-up land in Toruń and Bydgoszcz (Poland) 1975–2025 from Landsat with a Dynamic World-trained Random Forest: code and result data"
abstract: "Code (Google Colab notebook) and result data for reconstructing built-up land expansion in Toruń and Bydgoszcz, Poland, 1975–2025. A Random Forest classifier trained only on the Dynamic World built-up label of 2025 is applied without retraining to archival Landsat imagery (1985–2025) and, through a sensor bridge at the 1985 epoch, to Landsat MSS imagery (1975 and 1980). The series is validated against a static model on shared point panels and used for urban sprawl indicators, landscape metrics and the SDG 11.3.1 indicator (LCRPGR)."
